1) If a prototype is working on USB power but is resetting if connected to 12V, then the first thing I would do is check the voltage regulator used after the 12V, and compare it with 3.3V. A conventional USB charger will supply no more than 5 volts, so this tells us that the prototype is protected against high voltages, or the regulator is bad enough to not respond fast for suddent current draws and keeping a stable 3.3 volts, and this happens directly after the ESP32 tries to connect to the wifi, leading to this suddent high currrent draw. To  debug it I would test the regulator on its own, or try connecting a trusted regulator and see if the problem presists.
2) Hardware improvements: 
      Place a filter after the sensor
      Choose a high quality sensor
      Place the data cable perpendicular to any power cable to reduce electromagnetic interference
   Firmware improvements:
      Increase the sampling rate
      Filer the signal using a low pass filter
      Take the avarage of every 5 readings, and reject values that are logically not possible (they migh be caused due to hardware phenomenons)

3) In an industrial enclosure, machines will for sure block wifi from reaching every point in the industry. Machines can produce heat, magnetic fields, and their large size can block wifi signals. 
4) First, check if the device is recieving power, turned on , and giving any life signals. since the device is not sending data, a connection problem is a greate chance, the wifi connection should be reviewd. A briefe time logs could be added, like last succesfully sent data timing, and last unsuccessful data sending. A blinking LED when connected to wifi, and one blinking when sending data would be an indicator. For the remote diagnostic, a health message should be uploaded every 5 minutes, summarizing connection statues, sensor hardware status(if sending data or no), backend confirmation status, and memory status.
5) Before producing 20 boards, I would try the prototype in different settings that the PCBs might encounter  and test their performance in each, afterwhich I will test the wifi connection performance and the range of the connection. I will aslo test for different algorithms that might draw high currrent and account for that.


